g the words and phrases  that you have just learned  and it's extremely repetitive  so  each of the 10 cds here's one cd there's  10 of them in all  30 minutes each typically they will  cover  no sorry there's five cds and each seat  each lesson is i think 30 minutes long  i'm not entirely sure  um i should say that  uh since buying them i bought them on  wednesday today is friday  i've listened through just about all the  10 lessons there's a little bit in the  last lesson i haven't listened to  i listened mostly in my car i also  imported them into itunes and downloaded  them onto my ipod nano so that i could  listen while exercising  and while doing the dishes so basically  i've found the time to listen to  most of the lessons  um  you have the impression that each lesson  begins with a  very short dialogue two or three  sentences  uh and then those are broken up and  jumbled in different forms of it do you  wanna have lunch do you wanna have lunch  now do you wanna have lunch later do you  wanna have a drink do you wanna have a  drink at my place do you wanna drink at  your place do you wanna have a drink i  want to have a drink and just goes on  and on and on  uh so that  it's possible that these phrases because  now i've heard them you know over the  last  three days however much time that i've  spent however many hours that amounts to  these phrases just come back and back  and back  will they stick with me i don't know  it gives you a very painless  introduction to some of the  idiosyncrasies of the language but  there's a limit to what you can cover  and and in fact  pimsleur covers very very little i'm not  the first person to comment on this  there is very little vocabulary there  um  i think in the first lesson which cost  me 27  uh basically what we've covered is do  you understand romanian do you  understand english yes no  uh do you want to have a drink do you  want to have dinner with me at my  apartment or in a restaurant  where is plo pilar boulevard where is  eminescu street  you know and and and  they go to great lengths to help you  with the pronunciation even for things  like plopilar boulevard  plopilar lar lilar plopilar  you know and locular boulevard is not  something that i consider all that  useful  so uh and there's you know there's a lot  of effort to make it simple like aichi  is  is here  este  is is here  and then they'll say notice that the  words kind of run onto each other este  which they don't really do any more than  most words where there are two vowels in  any language will tend to run on a  little bit and they must mention that  three or four times so there's a lot of  superfluous  advice and and english and so forth so  to my mind  uh i i want to see  the advantage is that i've had a  painless introduction to romanian  and probably having listened to all that  romanian because the other the other  source that i'm going to go at together  with link is this teach yourself whoops  let's get it on the right side of me  well that's not very good there we go  and i mean just in reading the first  three four lessons of teach yourself  i have covered more vocabulary than is  covered in the whole of pimsleur  so if i were to continue with pinster i  mean i would have to spend an awful lot  of time listening  and  that's the other point in pipster why is  there no  transcript i can't understand why they  wouldn't provide a transcript  maybe it's because it would become too  obvious to people  that there is very little uh vocabulary  there but if i hear you know  intelligent into what it is  i can't really make out the sound  because i'm not used to listening to  romanian if i could read it  and i kind of looked at how these uh you  know how the romanian you know spelling  works  i'd have a much better chance of  remembering it remembering the  vocabulary and remembering the  pronunciation at least the way the way i  learned so  to my mind it's a bit frustrating that  there is no there are no transcripts  also  pimpster is based on the idea that if  there's a space repetition it's going to  help you learn  um in the short term i'm not finding  that to be the case uh when they prompt  me to say something i'm not able to say  even something that's been repeated now  since the first lesson i still can't do  it i can't respond that quickly  you know i believe that it just takes  time for the brain to get used to a  language  and  i don't see the benefit in having this  spaced repetition  within this artificial and very boring  and uninteresting context  it seems to me it would be better to  get going with  more in with denser content  keeping it simple  where you are listening only to the  target language  but you're covering more and more  material so you are  in fact achieving this based repetition  because all of the most common words and  phrases are going to come up very often  in most contexts so that there's no need  you know it's more it's almost spaced  repetition if you're studying you know  vocabulary lists so pimster is almost  like a vocabulary list but if you have  meaningful contexts which pimster  doesn't provide  meaningful and interesting context you  know within a month or two  i mean this is the other thing about  romanian you can read the newspaper very  quickly because the difficult thing in  the romanian in romanian is the  day-to-day conversation in the newspaper  uh i downloaded some items  into into link from newspapers  you know the director of the bureau  announced that there will be an  investigation into the situation all the  words they use are words that we're used  to from english so that the it's not  difficult i think to get into  more advanced material in romanian  pretty quickly once you figure out the  if and then by because and some of the  phrase forms which are  non-intuitive but but my repetitive  listening to pimsleur hasn't made them  any more intuitive they're still a bit  of a black box for me if i were able to  read them  uh  read them in different contexts i think  would be more more meaningful to me  so uh i don't want to be too negative on  on pimsleur here i sound negative i'm  telling you exactly how i react i react  the way i react because of the way i  like to study i like to study from  meaningful context i like to read  as well as listen i need them both  pimster doesn't provide that i'm not  convinced that this artificial space  repetition within that system  is effective  but it is pleasing it is easy  i'm sure that that the  large amount of english that's in there  is comforting to most learners  who are not  so keen to get totally thrown into the  target language  uh if you're in a hurry to learn the  language  um i don't think hempster is the way to  go uh as an icebreaker uh i think it's  it's good it's easy uh and and uh you  know this is the part that i have  trouble measuring when i go back to  reading and i will also do a review of  of the teacher's help book uh  reading the teach yourself book before i  did pimsleur which i did  and then having done a bunch of pimsleur  listening when i go to read in the teach  yourself again it's more alive to me now  because i've heard it in action now  is that because i was hearing it is it  because of pimsleur if i had had  the cd  that goes with future self would i have  had the same  you know pick up through listening  uh when i go back to reading i don't  know  so um you know a lot of these things are  hard to gauge i know that uh when i was  doing russian  a lot of material that i listened to  very very repetitively  those phrases stayed with me  for years they would be the easiest  phrases that i could call on  so there is an advantage in repetitive  listening uh however i don't understand  why they don't reinforce it with writing  and uh  you know as manfred spitzer said in his  book the brain requires repetition but  the brain also requires novelty  interest  and there's relatively little novelty in  pimpster i